{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SE5V6ejsqx4Pb7ZQzZWbTB","type":"tool_result","content":"  316 cycle/README.md\n  178 CONVENTIONS.md\n  131 AGENTS.md\n  625 total\n180:## Git and commits\n181-\n182-One branch per story or per fix cycle. Commit message: `<type>: <description>`, one line, in English,\n183-whatever the language of the session or of the file changed; the types are `feat`, `fix`,\n184-`refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`. The message states the resulting behaviour, never\n185-the process that produced it: no work-package reference, no review round, no attribution, no\n186-`Co-Authored-By`. Nothing is pushed by an automaton; `gh` for every GitHub operation, never the API\n187-directly; no issue is created by an automaton.\n188-\n189-## What is written by hand, and what is observed\n190-\n191-By hand: a product decision in `specs/adr/`, the order of the work in `specs/plan.yaml`, where\n192-the owner marks `prete: oui` the epics that run without them, and, for every epic added to the plan,\n193-its dossier in `specs/epics/`, which the plan entry cites as `source:` and the session that writes\n194-its stories reads. The story and the registry entry are\n195-written by hand when the owner drives the story; in a run without them, a session writes them under\n196-the rules of this file. Everything else is observed and recorded by the tool at the moment it\n197-observes it: a red and its message, a Preflight and its revision, a review round and its findings,\n198-the acceptance run and the owner's agreement, the landing. Evidence is written once, in the record of\n199-the step that produced it; elsewhere it is cited. A copy drifts from the code it describes.\n200-\n201-## The cycle without the owner\n202-\n203-`npm run cycle -- suite` runs, one after the other, the epics that `specs/plan.yaml` marks\n204-`prete: oui`, in the order of the plan. For each: the next story of the plan is written by a session\n20